 "caveats": [
  "A prefix's PoP is the one Starlink assigns that address block to; it does not reliably predict which PoP a given user's traffic leaves through.",
  "Before October 2025 Starlink published no PoP list; PoP mappings from then (e.g. in clarkzjw/starlink-geoip-data's geoip/ directory) came from DNS PTR records, which were often stale.",
  "The feed's city is the region Starlink sells into, not always a real town (mines, research stations), and customers can be hundreds of km away from it.",
  "PoP locations are their IATA airport's coordinates, not the facility's."
 ]
